      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-06T01:09:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They will be ordered on a single module and on dependencies, but not on other arbitrary modules.  Modules will be parsed and caught up to the current mutator at the point they are first added as a dependency.  They also won\u0027t have a full list of variants, just the variants required by the modules that depend on them that have been parsed.",
      "parentUuid": "524b00b1_09c8fb40",
      "revId": "454fc0a52f94e335ef928d2694402b09fa4ba7aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e09a4ae_625ba3e0",
        "filename": "cc/library_sdk_member.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-11T00:19:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027d be possible to handle with a variant-less module to use for the variant existence queries. No idea if something similar can be done in Bazel though. The only other option is to eliminate all OtherModule*Exists calls, then. Is that the plan?\n\nI don\u0027t have any good ideas what to do here. Even if I extract the logic that decides the variants from sdkMutator I can\u0027t call it from a different module here, and I don\u0027t see any way to test a predicate (e.g. through a provider interface) on all variants. What do you suggest?",
      "parentUuid": "960ab6e9_93c600f6",
      "revId": "454fc0a52f94e335ef928d2694402b09fa4ba7aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
